---
/**
 * Home page.
 *
 * NOTE: this file deliberately does NOT import or render `Disclaimer`.
 * `Base.astro` does. That is the P01 acceptance check — a page whose author
 * never thought about the disclaimer still shows it — and it is asserted in
 * `src/layouts/Base.test.ts`. If you came here to add the disclaimer because
 * you could not find it, it is already on the page; look at the layout.
 *
 * There are no tax figures on this page, and there will not be until the data
 * files land in P03. Every rupee amount, rate and threshold needs a citation to
 * primary law (CLAUDE.md rule 1), and the honest thing to show before the data
 * exists is nothing.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Sri Lanka Tax Return Support"
  description="Work out your Sri Lankan income tax and see exactly how the figure was reached, with the law behind every rate cited."
>
  <div class="intro measure">
    <h1>Work out what you owe, and check the working</h1>

    <p class="intro__lede">
      For individuals in Sri Lanka who have to work out their own income tax — often for
      the first time, and often without an employer or a practitioner in between.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <p>
      You choose a year of assessment, answer questions about your own circumstances in
      ordinary language, and get a computed liability with every step of the calculation
      shown and every rate linked to the provision it comes from.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing you enter leaves your browser. There is no account, no server, and no record
      of your figures.
    </p>

    <h2>What it will not do</h2>
    <p>
      Where the law is genuinely unclear about how a situation is treated, this tool says
      so and declines to produce a number, rather than picking the most plausible reading
      and presenting it as an answer. A refusal sends you to someone who can help; a
      confident wrong figure sends you to the Inland Revenue Department with a wrong
      return.
    </p>
    <p>
      It also will not suggest ways to reduce what you owe. It describes what the law
      provides, and what your figures produce under it.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it has got to</h2>
    <p>
      This is an early build. The page shell and its design tokens exist; the tax data,
      the calculation engine and the guidance pages are still being written. No figure
      appears anywhere yet, because no figure has a source behind it yet.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Every value resolves to a token from src/styles/global.css. */
  .intro h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    line-height: var(--text-3xl--line-height);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-block: 0 calc(var(--spacing) * 4);
  }

  .intro h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: var(--text-xl--line-height);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-block: calc(var(--spacing) * 10) calc(var(--spacing) * 3);
  }

  .intro__lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--text-lg--line-height);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .intro p {
    margin-block: 0 calc(var(--spacing) * 4);
  }
</style>
